      "id": "u17-1",
      "title": "Diminutives: -tjie, -ie, -jie, -pie",
      "explanation": [
        "Afrikaans speakers love making words \"little\": for size, cuteness, or friendliness. The ending depends on how the word ends:",
        "| word ends in | add | examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| -d, -t | **-jie** | hond → **hondjie**, kat → **katjie** |\n| -m | **-pie** | boom → **boompie** |\n| -k, -p, -s, -g | **-ie** | boek → **boekie**, kop → **koppie**, vis → **vissie** |\n| -l, -n, -r, a vowel | **-tjie** | tafel → **tafeltjie**, deur → **deurtjie**, vrou → **vroutjie** |\n| short vowel + -n, -l | double + **-etjie** | man → **mannetjie** |",
        "New words: **kyk** (look), **boom** (tree), **kop** (head), **vis** (fish). **Koppie** also means *cup*!"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Kyk die klein hondjie!",
          "en": "Look at the little dog!"
        },
        {
          "af": "Die kinders speel met die katjie.",
          "en": "The children are playing with the kitten."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek het 'n boompie.",
          "en": "I have a little tree."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "kyk",
        "boom",
        "kop",
        "vis"
      ],
