    {
      "id": "u17-2",
      "title": "Describing things",
      "explanation": [
        "After the noun, an adjective never changes: **Die man is vriendelik.**",
        "Before the noun, longer adjectives usually add **-e**: **'n vriendelike man**, **'n lelike hond**.",
        "Short, common ones often stay the same: **'n groot huis**, **'n mooi kar**, **'n klein kind**.",
        "Some change shape: **oud → ou** (die ou man), **nuut → nuwe** (die nuwe kar), **goed → goeie** (goeie môre!).",
        "Comparing: **groot → groter → grootste**, **mooi → mooier → mooiste**, **goed → beter → beste**. **as** = than. **vriend** = friend."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Ek het 'n nuwe kar.",
          "en": "I have a new car."
        },
        {
          "af": "Die ou man is baie vriendelik.",
          "en": "The old man is very friendly."
        },
        {
          "af": "My broer is groter as ek.",
          "en": "My brother is bigger than me."
        },
        {
          "af": "Hy is my beste vriend.",
          "en": "He is my best friend."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "oud",
        "nuut",
        "vriendelik",
        "lelik",
        "mooi",
        "as",
        "vriend"
      ],
